{
  "analysis": "My image is very close but has small off-by-1 differences in some pixels. I need to verify the exact float constants used by the binary, as my manual hex-to-float conversions may have errors. Let me write a small helper program to decode all the rodata constants precisely.",
  "plan": "Write and run a small C program that interprets the rodata hex values as floats, so I can get the exact constants for the ray direction, progress, and scaling formulas. Then update mystery.c accordingly.",
